>>- SC2016 1:6 -- \$HOME is literal in double quotes as well, so the single quotes hide no expansion

### braced expansion without its closing brace
echo 'Usage: ${name'
>>- SC2016 1:6 -- ${name without } is a syntax error in double quotes, not an expansion

### command substitution without its closing parenthesis
echo '$(ls'
>>- SC2016 1:6 -- $( without ) is a syntax error in double quotes, not an expansion

### double dollar before a word
echo 'pid $$foo'
>>- SC2016 1:6 -- $$ is the process ID and foo stays literal, so no variable foo is hidden

